before:
This local Node example deliberately uses the wrong operation.
```javascript
function total(price, quantity) {
  const result = price + quantity;
  debugger;
  return result;
}
console.log(total(4, 3));
```

after:
This example adds when it should multiply.

```javascript
function total(price, quantity) {
  const result = price + quantity;
  debugger;
  return result;
}
console.log(total(4, 3));
```

The debugger statement marks the pause when a debugger is attached.
